| “deliver food from the kitchen to an inpatient room”                                                                  | Goal     | This is a desired state/function of the system: food reaches the inpatient room. It states what should be achieved without fully fixing one delivery method. |
| “The delivery is made on an order-by-order basis in response to kitchen delivery requests”                            | Task     | This specifies a particular operational way of performing food delivery: handling each delivery request order by order.                                      |
| “kitchen delivery requests”                                                                                           | Resource | This is an informational entity needed to trigger the delivery process; the concern is whether such requests are available to the robot/system.              |
| “The food can be delivered into a room table by the robot”                                                            | Task     | This is a concrete alternative way of achieving food delivery: the robot places the food on the room table.                                                  |
| “requires a special manipulation robot skill”                                                                         | Resource | The manipulation skill is a required capability/resource; the concern is whether the robot has this skill available.                                         |
| “the food can be fetched from the robot's tray”                                                                       | Task     | This is another concrete alternative way of completing delivery: someone retrieves the meal from the robot tray.                                             |
| “Fetching from the robot tray requires cooperation with the inpatient, a companion, a nurse, or another robot”        | Task     | This specifies a particular collaborative procedure for completing tray-based delivery.                                                                      |
| “the inpatient”                                                                                                       | Resource | The inpatient can be needed as a cooperating participant for fetching food; the concern is whether the inpatient is able and available to cooperate.         |
| “a companion”                                                                                                         | Resource | The companion may be needed to retrieve the food; the concern is whether such a person is present and available.                                             |
| “a nurse”                                                                                                             | Resource | The nurse may be needed as a cooperating participant; the concern is whether the nurse is available at delivery time.                                        |
| “another robot”                                                                                                       | Resource | Another robot may be required to cooperate in fetching food, dish retrieval, or door opening; the concern is whether it is available.                        |
| “Some inpatients could be unable to fetch the food from the tray”                                                     | Belief   | This is domain knowledge explaining why assisted or alternative delivery strategies may be needed.                                                           |
| “a companion visitor or nurse could not be available at the moment of the delivery”                                   | Belief   | This captures a domain assumption/rationale about possible unavailability of human helpers.                                                                  |
| “The information about if the inpatient, a companion visitor or nurse can be able to retrieve the food from the tray” | Resource | This is informational content needed for deciding whether tray retrieval is feasible.                                                                        |
| “the inpatient record”                                                                                                | Resource | The inpatient record is an informational resource used to determine whether the patient or others can retrieve the meal.                                     |
| “information about the patient”                                                                                       | Resource | This information is needed to assess the patient’s ability to retrieve food from the robot tray.                                                             |
| “the presence of a companion into the room”                                                                           | Resource | This is information about whether a helper is available in the room, which affects the delivery strategy.                                                    |
| “This information is subject to uncertainty”                                                                          | Belief   | This is a domain characteristic affecting decision-making; it explains that available information may be unreliable or incomplete.                           |
| “The robot can carry multiple meals”                                                                                  | Belief   | This states an assumed capability of the robot and explains why meal identification and tracking are necessary.                                              |
| “multiple meals”                                                                                                      | Resource | Meals are physical entities carried and delivered by the robot; the concern is their availability, identity, and correct retrieval.                          |
| “the robot should indicate which meal should be retrieved by a given inpatient”                                       | Task     | This specifies a concrete system action to support correct meal retrieval.                                                                                   |
| “a given inpatient”                                                                                                   | Resource | The inpatient identity is needed to associate the correct meal with the correct recipient.                                                                   |
| “It should track when and where each meal was retrieved”                                                              | Task     | This specifies a concrete monitoring/logging function performed by the system.                                                                               |
| “when and where each meal was retrieved”                                                                              | Resource | This is informational data that must be captured and made available for traceability.                                                                        |
| “The robot should alert if a wrong meal is retrieved”                                                                 | Task     | This is a specific system behavior: detecting and alerting when an incorrect meal is taken.                                                                  |
| “Dirty dishes should be retrieved from the room”                                                                      | Goal     | This is a desired state of affairs: dirty dishes are removed from the inpatient room. The statement does not require one fixed method.                       |
| “the dish retrieve can occur unassisted”                                                                              | Task     | This is a specific way of achieving dirty dish retrieval without cooperation.                                                                                |
| “with the cooperation of two robots”                                                                                  | Task     | This specifies a concrete collaborative method for retrieving dishes.                                                                                        |
| “with the cooperation of robots and a human”                                                                          | Task     | This specifies another concrete collaborative method for retrieving dishes.                                                                                  |
| “Opening the room door”                                                                                               | Goal     | Door opening is a desired enabling condition for delivery or dish retrieval; multiple ways of achieving it are allowed.                                      |
| “can involve cooperation with another robot or a human”                                                               | Task     | This describes a particular way of opening the door through cooperation.                                                                                     |
| “another robot or a human”                                                                                            | Resource | These are cooperating participants that may be required to open the door; the concern is whether they are available.                                         |
| “Someone in the room can call a robot to pick up the dishes”                                                          | Task     | This specifies a concrete interaction procedure for initiating dish pickup.                                                                                  |
| “Someone in the room”                                                                                                 | Resource | This person is a possible initiator of dish pickup and may also support door opening; the concern is whether such a person is present and able.              |
| “call a robot to pick up the dishes”                                                                                  | Task     | This is a specific way to trigger the dish retrieval process.                                                                                                |
| “that person can signal if they can open the door when the robot comes to it”                                         | Task     | This specifies a concrete communication action that informs the robot whether human-assisted door opening is possible.                                       |
